{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run2:labor:historian","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:3038ee2579ecad9736a75552fee10a4bcb1bdc670ad12c092ad1015f1d5e72eb","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"binary","positiveOutcomeId":"yes","probability":0.22},"questionHash":"sha256:cfe468fa9439bedeee3804a35583667745f13831322e2c91a89c02a1b211413b","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq5","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"Conjunct A (MOVE 2027-2036 average >= 105): REFERENCE CLASS = MOVE history. Secondary sources put the long-run average at 93.6 since 1988 (ICE's own data page says history from 1996, so the start date is contested — flagging that), the 10-year average at ~75 (Carmignac), the 2017-2019 average at ~55, and the 2022 cycle at ~130. A threshold of 105 is therefore materially ABOVE the full-history mean. Reconstructing 10-year window averages: the late-1980s/1990s windows (~105-115) clear it, the 2000s (~95) borderline-fail, the 2010s (~70-80) fail badly, and 2017-2026 (~95-100) is borderline. That is roughly 6-8 of ~28 windows, ~22-28%. Adjusting up for the purely arithmetic content of 2A (far larger duration supply, net interest 2% -> 3% of GDP, levered basis-trade absorption replacing price-insensitive convenience-yield demand — all mechanical, not AI-specific), marginal A = 0.35. Conjunct B (>= one MSCI World >= 25% peak-to-trough drawdown in 2027-36 WITH G7 10y nominals failing to fall >= 50bp, or rising >= 25bp, in that window): REFERENCE CLASS = world-equity drawdowns >= 25% since 1970: 1973-74, 1980-82, 1987, 1990, 2000-02, 2007-09, 2020, 2022 — about 8 in 56 years, roughly one per 7 years, so P(at least one in a 10-year window) ~0.80-0.85 and the Poisson intensity is lambda ~1.4 per decade. CONDITIONAL FREQUENCY THAT BONDS FAILED TO RALLY >= 50bp: the correlated regime is 1973-74, 1980-82 and 2022 (yields rose through the drawdown) versus the flight-to-quality regime in 1987, 1990, 2000-02, 2008-09 and 2020 — 3 of 8, ~38%. Compounding over the decade: 1 - exp(-1.4 x 0.38) = 0.41, so marginal B = 0.40. CORRELATION: strongly positive, and I used ~+0.5 — a high-MOVE decade IS the inflation/term-premium regime in which sovereigns stop hedging equities, so P(B|A) rises from 0.40 to ~0.62. JOINT = 0.35 x 0.62 = 0.217 -> 22. OBSERVED vs INFERRED: the drawdown and conditional-failure frequencies are observed history; the +0.5 correlation and the upward tilt on A are inferred.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:55.251Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"OECD Earnings/Health at a Glance data show the OECD-average real hourly wage of personal-care and LTC workers rising >= 12% cumulatively ABOVE the whole-economy average between 2025 and 2030, reversing the Beyond Applause below-average finding.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031 (publication of the 2030 reference year)\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Directly falsifies my central claim that administered care wages cannot clear without a fiscal transfer 2A says is strained. CQ1's wage-divergence conjunct moves from 0.20 to ~0.40 and CQ1 from 12 to ~25-28; hypothesis plank (a) moves from 5 to ~20; CQ6-C gains ~3pp from B on the Baumol-cost channel.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"In any OECD country-year, the share of new RN or LPN licensees aged 40+ exceeds 15% (versus a historical ~6-8%), or a national statistical agency publishes a flow showing >= 10% of workers exiting ISIC J/K/M entering ISIC Q within three years.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the stock-flow mismatch and the ~0.05-0.10 cross-elasticity that drive my low CQ1 and my 5 on plank (a). Plank (a) moves to ~25-30, CQ1's second conjunct to ~0.32, CQ1 to ~16-18, and CQ3's P50 rises ~0.15pp because the care supply wall is the main non-AI constraint in my growth arithmetic.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Philippine BPO headcount (IBPAP/PSA) prints a year-over-year decline >= 5% in any single year, OR Indian IT-BPM export revenue (NASSCOM, nominal USD) declines in two consecutive years.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Breaks the ~0-of-3 base rate on which I rest my 14 for plank (b). Plank (b) moves from 14 to ~35-40, the virtual leg's loss moves to the upper end (-$160B/yr India, -550k Philippine jobs), and because the displaced pool widens, my J/K/M-side compression assumption strengthens: CQ1's wage conjunct falls further to ~0.15 and CQ1 to ~9.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"The OECD-38 harmonised unemployment rate prints no monthly value above 5.5% in any month from Jan 2027 through Dec 2030, and the 2027-2030 average is <= 5.2%.\",\"by_when\":\"Mar 31, 2031 (release of Dec 2030 data)\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Shows my ~50-55% per-window recession discount is too heavy and that the shrinking-labour-force denominator dominates. CQ1 conjunct A moves from 0.40 to ~0.65 and CQ1 from 12 to ~20; CQ3's P10 rises from 1.0 to ~1.3; CQ6-D falls ~4pp into B.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"The ICE BofA MOVE index averages >= 110 for both calendar 2028 and calendar 2029 while the G7 GDP-weighted 10y real yield averages >= 2.75% over the same two years.\",\"by_when\":\"Jan 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my mean-reversion-and-repression anchor on CQ4 and my below-mean read of MOVE. CQ4 P50 moves from 2.0% to ~2.6% with P90 to ~3.9%; CQ5 moves from 22 to ~40 (conjunct A to ~0.65); CQ6-C gains ~5pp and CQ6-A loses ~3pp on the debt-service arithmetic.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 1 historian seat, effort 'labor'."}}